  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759245,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 101-in-1 Explosive Megamix (Nintendo Wii)\n\nPrepare for a chaotic explosion of mini-game madness with *101-in-1 Explosive Megamix* on Nintendo Wii! Developed by Nordcurrent and originally released in Europe on September 22, 2011, this compilation delivers a staggering 101 diverse and frantic minigames across various genres, from puzzling challenges to sporty competitions and fast-paced arcade action. \n\nWhile marketed as a value-packed experience offering ten hours of gameplay, the WiiWare version received overwhelmingly negative reviews, largely due to repetitive gameplay, uninspired music, and frustrating controls. It's a direct port from the Nintendo DS and iPhone versions. Despite the sheer volume of games, critics found the overall quality lacking, with many comparing the experience to a Flash game. \n\nPlayers can enjoy a single-player experience or challenge friends locally via wireless play. Though boasting a wide variety of mini-games, the WiiWare release ultimately failed to impress, earning it a place among the lowest-rated games on Metacritic."
    },
